<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Gaston Browne</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">b. 1967</span> · <a href="/centuries/21st-century">21st century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Gaston Browne is a politician from Antigua and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/barbuda">Barbuda</a> who has been prime minister since 2014, leading the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/antigua-labour-party">Antigua and Barbuda Labour Party</a>. His governments oversaw the recovery after <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hurricane-irma">Hurricane Irma</a> devastated Barbuda in 2017, and faced controversy over changes to communal land ownership on Barbuda.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/gaston-browne.jpg" alt="Gaston Browne" width="320" height="427" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Ian Jones · CC BY 2.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Gaston_Browne_Buckingham_Palace_reception_(3x4_cropped).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
